  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sheru Nawab Pathan And Anr vs The State Of Maharashtra on 30 September, 2021 Author: Revati Mohite Dere Bench: Revati Mohite Dere Digitally signed by Nisha Nisha Sandeep Sandeep Chitnis Date: 2021.10.04 Chitnis 12:11:02 +0530 32 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Bail Application No.3281 Of 2021 1. Sheru Nawab Pathan 2. Mohammad Asif Abdul Jabbar Kachliya ...Applic Versus State of Maharashtra ...Respon Mr. Tushar Sonawane, for the Applicants.",
    "facts": "2. By this application, the applicants seek their enl bail in connection with C.R. No. 1094 of 2021 registered with the S Police Station, Solapur (Rural), for the alleged offence punishable Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 of the Indian Penal Code and under Sect 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. According to the complainant Sheru Nawab Pathan And Anr vs The State Of Maharashtra on 30 September, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/171074359/ 1 Bhuse, a Food and Safety Officer, he received a confidential inform N. S. Chitnis 32-ba.3281.2 with respect to one vehicle carrying prohibited material i.e. gutka, pan masala, tobacco etc. Accordingly, on 1st September 2021, one vehicle i.e Ashok Leyland Truck bearing No.MH-20 EL-5849 was intercepted. The applicant No.1 was the driver and owner on the said vehicle and the applicant No.2 was accompanying the applicant No.1. It was found that th applicants were carrying prohibited material in the said vehicle i.e. Hi Pan Masala valued at Rs.4,29,002/- and Royal 717 Scented Tobacco valued at Rs.2,31,003/-. Accordingly, the said articles were seized by the poli and the aforesaid C.R. was registered.",
    "arguments": "4. Learned Counsel for the applicants submits that prima facie taking the case as it stands, no offence as alleged under Section 328 of I.P.C is disclosed qua the applicants. He submits that as far as the oth sections are concerned, all the sections are bailable.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. Learned Counsel for the applicants submits that prima facie taking the case as it stands, no offence as alleged under Section 328 of I.P.C is disclosed qua the applicants. He submits that as far as the oth sections are concerned, all the sections are bailable.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
